{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall make atonement for him, etc., and it shall be forgiven him.</b> From heaven — for the sin is nullified together with the offering by the Holy One, blessed be He, and this is the sense of וכפר from the root of (Genesis 32:21) ״אכפרה פניו״ (I will appease his face). But complete forgiveness is not entrusted to flesh and blood, but to the Holy One, blessed be He, alone, as it is written (Psalms 130:4) ״כי עמך הסליחה״ — for with You is forgiveness. And so you will find this expression in all of them — <b>and the priest shall make atonement for him and it shall be forgiven him</b> — except for the oath of utterance, where it says there only וכפר עליו הכהן מחטאתו, and it does not say ונסלח לו."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:01.573233230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}